{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012NE9DQKWmfafMJ3CK19tpg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 09 -- Verifier stage, report rendering, text sanitization\n2\t\n3\t## 1. Purpose\n4\t\n5\tThis area covers the three steps between the finder and the run record:\n6\t\n7\t1. The **verifier** stage. Every finding the finder kept is adjudicated by\n8\t   the verifier role's model, which sees the claim and the code only, never\n9\t   the finder's reasoning (anti-anchoring). A refutation counts only when it\n10\t   is grounded in specific code, guards, or language semantics. Anything the\n11\t   verifier cannot decide fails open: the finding keeps gating, with the\n12\t   reason on its verdict.\n13\t2. **Report rendering.** A completed review becomes a JSON payload (stdout,\n14\t   and `result.json` in the run record) and a Markdown summary (stderr, and\n15\t   `report.md` in the run record).\n16\t3. **Text sanitization** (`textsafe`). Finding text comes from a model that\n17\t   read an untrusted repository, so a JSON string such as `\"\\u001b]52;c;...\"`\n18\t   decodes to a real ESC. Every place Roast prints model- or\n19\t   repository-derived text to a terminal or into a human-readable report\n20\t   escapes control characters first. JSON output does not go through it.\n21\t\n22\tOut of scope here (owned by other areas): the finder, prompt texts and the\n23\tverifier user-prompt renderer, exploration tools, the agent loop\n24\t(`Converse`), the token ledger internals, finding fingerprints, prior\n25\tsightings lookup, run-record file writing, and CLI flag parsing in general.\n26\t\n27\tNotation: in quoted output strings below, `{EM}` stands for one literal\n28\tU+2014 EM DASH character, which the Go output contains and the TypeScript\n29\toutput must contain too. `·` is U+00B7 MIDDLE DOT, also literal.\n30\t\n31\t## 2. Behavior contract\n32\t\n33\t### 2.1 Data model used by this area\n34\t\n35\tOwned by the review area; restated here because rendering and verification\n36\tdepend on every field.\n37\t\n38\tSeverity: one of `INFO`, `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL`. `rank`:\n39\tINFO=0, LOW=1, MEDIUM=2, HIGH=3, CRITICAL=4; any other string (including\n40\t`\"\"`) ranks 0. `parseSeverity(s)` upper-cases and trims (Go\n41\t`strings.TrimSpace`), accepts only the five names, rejects `\"\"`.\n42\t\n43\tFinding (JSON field order is significant for output parity):\n44\t\n45\t| key | type | notes |\n46\t| --- | --- | --- |\n47\t| `reasoning` | string | |\n48\t| `severity` | string | |\n49\t| `confidence` | number | |\n50\t| `cwe` | string | |\n51\t| `description` | string | |\n52\t| `file` | string | |\n53\t| `lines` | int[] or null | `null` when absent |\n54\t| `code_quote` | string | |\n55\t| `fixed_code` | string | |\n56\t| `frontend_category` | string | |\n57\t| `verdict` | Verdict | omitted when absent |\n58\t| `_drop_reason` | string | omitted when `\"\"` |\n59\t| `id` | string | omitted when `\"\"` |\n60\t| `alias` | string | omitted when `\"\"`, e.g. `R-8d8d19` |\n61\t\n62\tVerdict (field order significant):\n63\t\n64\t| key | type | notes |\n65\t| --- | --- | --- |\n66\t| `reasoning` | string | always present |\n67\t| `status` | string | `confirmed`, `refuted`, `insufficient_context` |\n68\t| `confidence` | number | always present |\n69\t| `grounding` | string | always present |\n70\t| `recalibrated_severity` | string | omitted when `\"\"` |\n71\t| `verifier` | string | omitted when `\"\"`; set by Roast (model id) |\n72\t| `undecided` | boolean | omitted when false; set by Roast |\n73\t\n74\t`verdict.gates()`: true when the verdict is absent or its status is not\n75\t`refuted`.\n76\t\n77\t`finding.effectiveSeverity()`: the finder's `severity`, unless the verdict\n78\texists, its status is `confirmed`, `parseSeverity(recalibrated_severity)`\n79\tsucceeds, and that parsed severity's rank is strictly lower than the\n80\tfinder's severity rank; then the parsed (canonical) severity. Severity can\n81\tonly move down, and only on a confirmed verdict.\n82\t\n83\tResult: `findings` (Finding[]), `dropped` (Finding[]), `assessment`\n84\t(string), `notes` (string[] or null), `incomplete` (boolean),\n85\t`stopReason` (string: `\"\"`, `deadline`, `token_budget`,\n86\t`budget_exhausted`).\n87\t\n88\t`result.maxSeverity()`: the highest `effectiveSeverity().rank` among\n89\t`findings` (live findings only), or -1 when there are none.\n90\t\n91\tDrop reasons: `invalid_severity`, `missing_code_quote`,\n92\t`missing_fixed_code`, `ungrounded_code_quote`, `below_confidence_floor`\n93\t(finder side) and `refuted_by_verifier` (this area).\n94\t\n95\tAssessments: `FINDINGS_PRESENT`, `NO_FINDINGS`, `NO_DIFF`,\n96\t`INCOMPLETE_NO_SUBMISSION`, `NO_FINDINGS_IN_SAMPLED_AREAS`.\n97\t\n98\t### 2.2 When verification runs\n99\t\n100\t- `doVerify = !quick && !noVerify` (`--quick`, `--no-verify`, both boolean,\n101\t  default false). When `doVerify` is true the verifier role is validated\n102\t  before anything else runs (config area; failure is a usage error, exit 2).\n103\t  With `--quick` or `--no-verify` the verifier role is never validated or\n104\t  contacted.\n105\t- The verifier client is constructed, and `verify` is called, only when\n106\t  `doVerify` is true **and** the finder returned at least one finding. With\n107\t  zero findings no verifier request is made, but the report still says\n108\t  `\"verified\": true` and `usage` has only a `finder` entry.\n109\t- Before calling `verify`, the CLI logs through its `logf` helper (one\n110\t  `roast: ...` line on stderr, sanitized with `textsafe.text`):\n111\t  `verifying <n> finding(s) with <model> (profile=<p> protocol=<proto>)`.\n112\t- The CLI calls `verify` with: system prompt = the rendered verifier system\n113\t  prompt; user prompt = the verifier user-prompt renderer for the finding\n114\t  (prompts area; it includes the cited file snippet, never the finder's\n115\t  reasoning); tools = the exploration tools over the reviewed tree (context\n116\t  area); `maxTurns = 8`; `maxVerified` = resolved cap; the run's shared\n117\t  token ledger; `log` writes the message plus `\\n` to stderr. Concurrency is\n118\t  not set by the CLI, so the default 4 applies.\n119\t- `maxVerified` resolution: `--max-verified` flag if given on the command\n120\t  line, else `limits.max_verified` from `.roast.json`, else 25. A negative\n121\t  flag value is a usage error `max-verified cannot be negative` (exit 2).\n122\t  `0` means no cap. The resolved value is recorded in budgets as\n123\t  `verifier_cap`.\n124\t- After `verify` returns, `usage.verifier` is the verifier client's usage.\n125\t  The run is **partial** if the finder result was `incomplete` or any\n126\t  surviving finding's verdict has `undecided: true`.\n127\t\n128\t### 2.3 `verify(signal, verifier, result, deps)` algorithm\n129\t\n130\tInputs: `deps.concurrency` (default 4 when `<= 0`), `deps.log` (default\n131\tno-op), `deps.userPrompt` (default returns `\"\"`), `deps.maxVerified`\n132\t(0 = no cap), `deps.ledger` (may be absent; absent is never exhausted).\n133\t\n134\t1. `n = result.findings.length`; allocate `verdicts[n]`.\n135\t2. Run a promise pool of `concurrency` workers over indices `0..n-1`,\n136\t   handed out in ascending index order. For the job at index `i`, at the\n137\t   moment a worker picks it up:\n138\t   1. If `maxVerified > 0 && i >= maxVerified`: verdict =\n139\t      `unverified(\"unverified: over the per-run verifier cap (<maxVerified>)\")`.\n140\t      The cap is by input position, so it is deterministic.\n141\t   2. Else if the ledger is exhausted: verdict =\n142\t      `unverified(\"unverified: run token budget exhausted before this\n143\t      finding's verification\")` (one line in the real string; the\n144\t      apostrophe is U+0027). The check is made at launch only;\n145\t      verifications already in flight finish normally.\n146\t   3. Else: verdict = `verifyOne(finding)`.\n147\t   4. Set `verdict.verifier = verifier.name()` (the verifier role's model\n148\t      id) on every verdict, including unverified and error verdicts.\n149\t   5. Store at `verdicts[i]`.\n150\t   `unverified(reason)` is `{status: \"insufficient_context\", undecided:\n151\t   true, reasoning: reason, confidence: 0, grounding: \"\"}`.\n152\t3. Wait for all workers. Then assemble a **new** result (the input is not\n153\t   mutated):\n154\t   - `dropped` = copy of input `dropped` (existing drops first).\n155\t   - `notes` = copy of input `notes`. Go quirk to preserve: an empty input\n156\t     notes list becomes `null` (Go `append(nil, empty...)` is nil), so a\n157\t     verified run with no notes serializes `\"notes\": null` (kept for\n158\t     Go parity; spec.md).\n159\t   - `assessment`, `incomplete`, `stopReason` copied unchanged (cutoff state\n160\t     survives verification).\n161\t   - `findings` = new empty list.\n162\t4. For each input finding in input order, with `v = verdicts[i]`:\n163\t   1. **Refutation without grounding:** if `v.status == \"refuted\"` and\n164\t      `goTrimSpace(v.grounding) == \"\"`, rewrite `v.status =\n165\t      \"insufficient_context\"`, `v.undecided = true`, `v.reasoning =\n166\t      \"verifier returned refuted without grounding {EM} treating as\n167\t      insufficient_context (fail-open)\"`. Confidence and grounding are\n168\t      kept as returned.\n169\t   2. **Ungrounded recalibration:** if `v.status == \"confirmed\"` and\n170\t      `v.recalibrated_severity != \"\"` and `goTrimSpace(v.grounding) == \"\"`,\n171\t      clear `recalibrated_severity` to `\"\"`.\n172\t   3. Attach `v` as the finding's verdict (copy of the finding).\n173\t   4. If `!v.gates()` (status still `refuted`): set `_drop_reason =\n174\t      \"refuted_by_verifier\"`, append to `dropped`, and call `deps.log` with\n175\t      `roast: verifier refuted [<SEV>] <DESC> (conf <C>)` where\n176\t      `<SEV> = textsafe.line(finding.severity)` (the finder's raw severity),\n177\t      `<DESC> = textsafe.line(truncateUtf8(finding.description, 80))`\n178\t      (truncate first, escape second), and `<C>` is `verdict.confidence`\n179\t      formatted as Go `%.2f` (section 2.9). Log lines are emitted in input\n180\t      order after all verifications finish, not as they complete.\n181\t   5. Else append to `findings`.\n182\t5. If `findings` is empty and `assessment == \"FINDINGS_PRESENT\"`, set\n183\t   `assessment = \"NO_FINDINGS\"`. No other assessment is changed (in\n184\t   particular `INCOMPLETE_NO_SUBMISSION` never becomes `NO_FINDINGS`).\n185\t6. Return the new result. Errors never propagate out of `verify`.\n186\t\n187\tRecalibrated severity is never applied to the finding's `severity` field;\n188\tit lives only on the verdict and takes effect through `effectiveSeverity()`\n189\t(rendering, sort order, `--max-severity`). The JSON output therefore keeps\n190\tthe finder's `severity` and shows `verdict.recalibrated_severity`\n191\talongside.\n192\t\n193\t`truncateUtf8(s, n)`: if the UTF-8 byte length of `s` is `<= n`, return\n194\t`s`; otherwise cut at byte `n`, moving the cut left while the byte at the\n195\tcut is a UTF-8 continuation byte (`0b10xxxxxx`), so a code point is never\n196\tsplit. Measured in UTF-8 bytes, not UTF-16 units.\n197\t\n198\t### 2.4 `verifyOne(finding)`\n199\t\n200\t- Tools sent: `deps.tools` in order, then the final tool appended last:\n201\t  - name `submit_verdict`\n202\t  - description `Submit your verdict on the finding. Call exactly once.`\n203\t  - no runner (it is the final tool; the agent loop ends on it)\n204\t  - schema: exactly the JSON below (Go reflects it and re-serializes through\n205\t    a map, so property keys are alphabetical in the transmitted bytes):\n206\t\n207\t```json\n208\t{\n209\t  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n210\t  \"properties\": {\n211\t    \"confidence\": {\"maximum\": 1, \"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"number\"},\n212\t    \"grounding\": {\n213\t      \"description\": \"<GROUNDING_DESC>\",\n214\t      \"type\": \"string\"\n215\t    },\n216\t    \"reasoning\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n217\t    \"recalibrated_severity\": {\n218\t      \"description\": \"<RECAL_DESC>\",\n219\t      \"enum\": [\"\", \"INFO\", \"LOW\", \"MEDIUM\", \"HIGH\", \"CRITICAL\"],\n220\t      \"type\": \"string\"\n221\t    },\n222\t    \"status\": {\n223\t      \"enum\": [\"confirmed\", \"refuted\", \"insufficient_context\"],\n224\t      \"type\": \"string\"\n225\t    }\n226\t  },\n227\t  \"required\": [\"reasoning\", \"status\", \"confidence\", \"grounding\"],\n228\t  \"type\": \"object\"\n229\t}\n230\t```\n231\t\n232\t  The two placeholders are these exact one-line strings (wrapped here\n233\t  only for width; join the pieces with a single space):\n234\t  - `<GROUNDING_DESC>`: `The exact lines / contradicting code /`\n235\t    `language-semantics fact the verdict rests on`\n236\t  - `<RECAL_DESC>`: `If the finding is real but its severity is`\n237\t    `overstated, the corrected LOWER severity, justified in grounding.`\n238\t    `Leave empty to keep the finder's severity. Never raise severity.`\n239\t    (the apostrophe is U+0027)\n240\t- The model-facing (\"wire\") verdict has only `reasoning`, `status`,\n241\t  `confidence`, `grounding`, `recalibrated_severity`. `verifier` and\n242\t  `undecided` are deliberately absent so the model cannot fabricate them.\n243\t- Call the agent loop: `converse(signal, systemPrompt, userPrompt(finding),\n244\t  {tools, finalTool: \"submit_verdict\", maxTurns: deps.maxTurns})`. A\n245\t  `maxTurns` of 0 means the agent loop's default; the CLI passes 8.\n246\t- On **any** error from the loop (no final call, schema violation of the\n247\t  final call, transport failure after retries, abort):\n248\t  return `{status: \"insufficient_context\", confidence: 0, reasoning:\n249\t  \"verifier did not reach a verdict: \" + err.message, grounding: \"\",\n250\t  undecided: true}`. The finding keeps gating.\n251\t- On success: copy the five wire fields into a verdict\n252\t  (`undecided` false, `verifier` set later by the pool).\n253\t\n254\t### 2.5 Output formats and destinations\n255\t\n256\t`--format` takes `json`, `markdown`, or `both` (default `both`). Any other\n257\tvalue is a usage error `invalid --format \"<value>\"` (Go `%q` quoting),\n258\texit 2.\n259\t\n260\t`writeReport`:\n261\t- `json` or `both`: `toJSON(report)` plus `\\n` to **stdout**.\n262\t- `markdown` or `both`: `toMarkdown(report, showDropped)` plus `\\n` to\n263\t  **stderr**.\n264\t- JSON is written before Markdown.\n265\t\n266\tRun record (records area writes the files; this area provides content):\n267\t- `result.json` = `toJSON(report)`.\n268\t- `report.md` = `toMarkdown(report, true)` -- dropped findings always\n269\t  included, independent of `--show-dropped`.\n270\t- `writeReport` runs before the run-record files are finalized.\n271\t- After finalization succeeds the CLI logs `run <id> · report <path>`.\n272\t\n273\t`--show-dropped` (boolean, default false) only affects the stderr Markdown.\n274\t\n275\tThere is no color, no ANSI styling, and no TTY detection in rendering;\n276\toutput is identical whether or not stdout/stderr are terminals.\n277\t\n278\tEmpty-scope path (`NO_DIFF`): when scope is empty, no model is called and\n279\tthe CLI writes a report with `result = {assessment: \"NO_DIFF\", findings:\n280\t[], dropped: [], notes: []}`, `mode: \"code\"`, `files_reviewed: []`, all\n281\tother report fields at zero values (no run id, `quick: false`,\n282\t`verified: false` even under `--quick`, `usage` and `prompt_packs` null),\n283\tthrough the same `writeReport`, and exits 0 regardless of\n284\t`--max-severity`. No run record is written.\n285\t\n286\t### 2.6 `--max-severity` and exit codes\n287\t\n288\t- `--max-severity` (string, default `\"\"`). Non-empty values go through\n289\t  `parseSeverity(value.toUpperCase())`; failure is a usage error\n290\t  `invalid --max-severity \"<value>\"` (exit 2). `gateRank` is the parsed\n291\t  rank, or -1 when the flag is empty.\n292\t- Exit decision after the report is written and the run record finalized,\n293\t  in priority order:\n294\t  1. Run-record finalization failed: that error (exit per the CLI error\n295\t     classification area).\n296\t  2. `gateRank >= 0 && result.maxSeverity() >= gateRank`: exit 1\n297\t     (`ExitFindings`). Uses effective (possibly recalibrated) severity of\n298\t     live findings only; dropped and refuted findings never trip it.\n299\t  3. Partial run (section 2.2): exit 4 (`ExitPartial`). Note that findings\n300\t     past the verifier cap or past ledger exhaustion are `undecided`, so\n301\t     they make the run partial.\n302\t  4. Otherwise exit 0.\n303\t\n304\t### 2.7 JSON report (`toJSON`)\n305\t\n306\t`Report` inputs: `result`, `mode`, `filesReviewed`, `task` (not rendered),\n307\t`runId`, `budgets` (object or absent), `quick`, `verified`,\n308\t`diffTruncated`, `originalDiffBytes`, `sizeBreakdown` (`{path, bytes}[]`),\n309\t`usage` (role name -> Usage, or absent), `prior` (fingerprint -> note, or\n310\tabsent), `promptPacks` (string[] or absent), and the survey fields\n311\t`reviewKind` (`\"survey_triage\"` or `\"\"`), `completion` (`partial` |\n312\t`complete`), `manifestFileCount`, `stopReason` (`converged` |\n313\t`budget_exhausted` | `incomplete_no_submission` | `deadline` |\n314\t`token_budget`).\n315\t\n316\tOutput is one compact JSON object (no whitespace, no trailing newline in the\n317\tstring itself). Go emits the top-level keys in **alphabetical order**\n318\t(it marshals a map); the TS version should build the object in the same\n319\tsorted order. Keys:\n320\t\n321\t| key | when present | value |\n322\t| --- | --- | --- |\n323\t| `assessment` | always | `result.assessment` |\n324\t| `budgets` | `budgets` set | the budgets object, nested keys sorted |\n325\t| `completion` | `reviewKind != \"\"` | `completion` |\n326\t| `diff_truncated` | `diffTruncated` | `true` |\n327\t| `dropped_findings` | always | `result.dropped` as finding-outs, or `[]` |\n328\t| `files_reviewed` | always | `filesReviewed` (`null` if absent) |\n329\t| `findings` | always | finding-out list of `result.findings`, `[]` when empty |\n330\t| `incomplete` | `result.incomplete` | `true` |\n331\t| `manifest_file_count` | `reviewKind != \"\"` | integer |\n332\t| `mode` | always | `mode` (`\"code\"` today) |\n333\t| `notes` | always | `result.notes` (`null` if absent, see 2.3) |\n334\t| `original_diff_bytes` | `diffTruncated` | integer |\n335\t| `prompt_packs` | always | `promptPacks` (`null` if absent) |\n336\t| `quick` | always | boolean |\n337\t| `review_kind` | `reviewKind != \"\"` | `\"survey_triage\"` |\n338\t| `run_id` | `runId != \"\"` | run id |\n339\t| `size_breakdown` | `diffTruncated` | `[{\"path\":..., \"bytes\":...}]` |\n340\t| `stop_reason` | see below | string |\n341\t| `usage` | always | object keyed by role (`finder`, `verifier`), or `null` |\n342\t| `verified` | always | boolean |\n343\t\n344\t`stop_reason`: when `reviewKind != \"\"` it is the report's `stopReason`\n345\t(survey block owns the key, possibly `\"\"`); otherwise it is\n346\t`result.stopReason`, present only when non-empty. A non-survey cut-off run\n347\twith retained findings thus carries both `incomplete: true` (when the loop\n348\tended without submission) and `stop_reason`.\n349\t\n350\tEach `usage` value: `{\"uncached_input_tokens\":int,\n351\t\"cached_input_tokens\":int, \"cache_write_tokens\":int, \"output_tokens\":int,\n352\t\"calls\":int}` in that order. Role keys sorted.\n353\t\n354\tFinding-out object: the Finding fields in the table order of section 2.1,\n355\tthen:\n356\t- `fingerprint`: the finding's fingerprint (review area), omitted only if\n357\t  empty;\n358\t- `prior_sighting`: `prior[fingerprint]` when `prior` has that key and the\n359\t  note is non-empty (omitted when empty).\n360\t\n361\t`budgets` content is built by the CLI area (`deadline_duration`,\n362\t`request_timeout` as Go duration strings, `max_total_tokens`,\n363\t`verifier_cap`, `max_turns`, `max_attempts`, `max_prompt_bytes`, and\n364\t`ledger_committed_tokens` when the ledger has a limit). The CLI adds\n365\t`ledger_committed_tokens` and sets `prior` after building the report but\n366\tbefore rendering, so both appear in output.\n367\t\n368\tJSON strings are never passed through `textsafe`: the JSON encoder escapes\n369\tC0 controls, so raw finding text round-trips exactly through\n370\t`JSON.parse`. Go's encoder additionally escapes `<`, `>`, `&` as\n371\t`\\u003c`/`\\u003e`/`\\u0026` and U+2028/U+2029; TS does not, and the differential\n372\tharness compares parsed JSON (spec.md, \"JSON encoding\").\n373\tNumbers: Go and JS agree on shortest round-trip float formatting\n374\t(exponent form below 1e-6 and from 1e21, `1e-7` style), so\n375\t`JSON.stringify` numbers match.\n376\t\n377\t### 2.8 Markdown report (`toMarkdown(report, showDropped)`)\n378\t\n379\tLines are collected into a list and joined with `\\n` (no trailing newline\n380\tadded beyond what an empty last line produces). Structure, in order:\n381\t\n382\t1. **Survey banner** (only when `reviewKind != \"\"`):\n383\t   `> Survey triage {EM} manifest contains <manifestFileCount> files,\n384\t   completion=<completion>, stop=<report.stopReason>` (one line), then `\"\"`.\n385\t2. Count `nRefuted` = dropped findings with `_drop_reason ==\n386\t   \"refuted_by_verifier\"`; `nMalformed = dropped.length - nRefuted`.\n387\t3. **Headline.** If `findings` is empty, the first matching case:\n388\t   1. `assessment == \"NO_DIFF\"`: `## Nothing to review in this scope {EM}\n389\t      no review ran`, `\"\"`, then one line (shown wrapped here; the three\n390\t      flag mentions are Markdown code spans with single backticks):\n391\t\n392\t      ```text\n393\t      No model was called, so this is NOT a clean review. Already\n394\t      committed? Try `--base <ref>`; use `--staged` before committing or\n395\t      `--scope repo` for a repository survey.\n396\t      ```\n397\t   2. `result.stopReason` is `deadline` or `token_budget`: `## Roast cut\n398\t      off early (<stopReason>) {EM} no findings before the cutoff`, `\"\"`,\n399\t      `The review was cut short by a run ceiling; this is NOT a clean\n400\t      review.`\n401\t   3. `assessment == \"INCOMPLETE_NO_SUBMISSION\"`: `## Roast incomplete\n402\t      {EM} no findings were submitted`, `\"\"`, `The interactive review\n403\t      exhausted its budget before submitting; this is NOT a clean review.`\n404\t   4. Otherwise: `## Roast complete {EM} no findings`, `\"\"`, then\n405\t      `The adversary found nothing to complain about.`, with\n406\t      ` (<nRefuted> candidate finding(s) were refuted by the cross-model\n407\t      verifier.)` appended on the same line when `nRefuted > 0`.\n408\t\n409\t   If `findings` is non-empty: when `result.stopReason != \"\"`, first\n410\t   `## Roast cut off early (<stopReason>) {EM} partial findings follow`\n411\t   and `\"\"`; then `## Roast: <n> finding(s)` with ` (cross-model\n412\t   verified)` appended when `report.verified`.\n413\t4. If `nMalformed > 0`: `\"\"`, then `*(<nMalformed> candidate(s) dropped by\n414\t   schema gates; --show-dropped to see them.)*`.\n415\t5. `\"\"`.\n416\t6. **Findings**, sorted with a stable sort: effective severity rank\n417\t   descending, then `confidence` descending; ties keep input order. Each\n418\t   rendered with ordinal `i+1` (1-based position after sorting) and\n419\t   `dropped = false`.\n420\t7. **Dropped section**, only when `showDropped` and `dropped` is non-empty:\n421\t   `## Dropped findings (--show-dropped)`, `\"\"`, then each dropped finding\n422\t   in stored order (finder drops first, then verifier refutations), ordinal\n423\t   `i+1`, `dropped = true`.\n424\t\n425\tThe `{EM}` dash in headings and `·` are literal; headline strings are\n426\totherwise plain ASCII. Nothing in the headline is model-derived except\n427\t`stopReason`, which is a fixed internal value.\n428\t\n429\t**Finding block** (`renderFinding(ordinal, finding, dropped, prior)`):\n430\t\n431\t- `sev = line(severity)`; if that is `\"\"`, `sev = \"INFO\"`. If\n432\t  `effectiveSeverity() != severity` (raw string comparison), `sev =\n433\t  \"<line(effective)> (finder claimed <sev> {EM} verifier recalibrated)\"`.\n434\t- `confStr = \" · conf <%.2f confidence>\"`.\n435\t- `tag = \"\"`, or when `dropped`: `\"[DROPPED:<line(reason)>] \"` where\n436\t  reason is `_drop_reason`, or `?` when empty.\n437\t- `path = file`, or `?` when empty (checked before escaping).\n438\t- `ln`: `?` for no lines; `<l0>` for one; `<first>-<last>` for more (first\n439\t  and last elements as given, not min/max).\n440\t- `desc = line(goTrimSpace(description))`.\n441\t- `handle = line(alias)`, or `<ordinal>.` when that is empty.\n442\t- Lines emitted:\n443\t  1. `### <handle> <tag>[<sev><confStr>] <desc>`\n444\t  2. `- **File:** ` + `inlineCode(line(path) + \":\" + ln)`\n445\t  3. only if raw `cwe != \"\"`: `- **CWE:** <line(cwe)>`\n446\t  4. `- **Reasoning:** <listItemText(reasoning, \"  \")>`\n447\t  5. if a verdict exists:\n448\t     `- **Verifier (<line(verifier) or ?>):** <line(status)> (conf <%.2f>)`;\n449\t     then, only if raw `grounding != \"\"`:\n450\t     `  - grounding: <listItemText(grounding, \"    \")>`\n451\t  6. For `(\"Current\", code_quote)` then `(\"Proposed fix\", fixed_code)`:\n452\t     `block = text(value)` with all trailing `\\n` removed. If `block` is\n453\t     non-empty: `- **<label>:**`, then `\"  \" + fence`, then each line of\n454\t     `block` (split on `\\n`) prefixed with two spaces, then\n455\t     `\"  \" + fence`, where `fence = codeFence(block)`. If `block` is empty\n456\t     and `dropped`: `- **<label>:** *(not provided)*`. If empty and not\n457\t     dropped: nothing.\n458\t  7. If `prior` has the finding's fingerprint:\n459\t     `- **Seen previously:** <line(note)>` (emitted even for an empty note).\n460\t  8. `\"\"`.\n461\t\n462\tHelpers:\n463\t- `listItemText(s, indent) = text(goTrimSpace(s))` with every `\\n`\n464\t  replaced by `\\n` + indent, so model text cannot leave its list item and\n465\t  pose as a heading.\n466\t- `codeFence(content)`: backticks repeated `max(3, longestBacktickRun +\n467\t  1)` times, so a quoted backtick run cannot close the block.\n468\t- `inlineCode(s)`: delimiter = backticks repeated `longestBacktickRun(s) +\n469\t  1`; if `s` starts or ends with a backtick, `delim + \" \" + s + \" \" +\n470\t  delim`, else `delim + s + delim`.\n471\t- `longestBacktickRun(s)`: longest run of consecutive `` ` `` characters.\n472\t\n473\t### 2.9 Go-compatible formatting helpers\n474\t\n475\t- `goTrimSpace(s)`: trim leading and trailing characters for which Go\n476\t  `unicode.IsSpace` is true: `\\t \\n \\v \\f \\r`, space, U+0085, U+00A0, and\n477\t  the Unicode `Zs`/line/paragraph separators (U+1680, U+2000-U+200A,\n478\t  U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000). It differs from JS\n479\t  `String.prototype.trim`: Go trims U+0085 (JS does not) and does not trim\n480\t  U+FEFF (JS does). Used for the grounding emptiness checks (2.3) and\n481\t  description/reasoning/grounding rendering (2.8), where parity matters.\n482\t- `formatFixed2(x)` (Go `%.2f`): Go rounds the exact binary value half-to-even,\n483\t  JS `toFixed(2)` rounds exact ties up. They differ only on exact ties,\n484\t  which for doubles are values where `x * 8` is an odd integer (0.125,\n485\t  0.375, 0.625, 0.875, ...): Go `0.12 0.38 0.62 0.88`, JS\n486\t  `0.13 0.38 0.63 0.88`. Implementation: if `Number.isInteger(x * 8) &&\n487\t  (x * 8) % 2 !== 0`, take `n = Math.floor(x * 100)` (exact), add 1 if `n`\n488\t  is odd, and format `n / 100` with `toFixed(2)`; otherwise `x.toFixed(2)`.\n489\t  Handle negatives symmetrically. Used in the verifier log line and in\n490\t  Markdown confidences.\n491\t\n492\t### 2.10 Text sanitization (`textsafe`)\n493\t\n494\tTwo modes over a sequence of decoded code points (Go: UTF-8 bytes):\n495\t\n496\t**`text(s)`** (multi-line):\n497\t- Byte that is not part of a valid UTF-8 sequence -> `\\xNN` (two lowercase\n498\t  hex digits of that byte). Each invalid byte is escaped individually (Go\n499\t  `DecodeRune` returns size 1 for any invalid or truncated sequence, so\n500\t  `\"\\xe2\\x82\"` -> `\\xe2\\x82`). Overlong encodings, UTF-8-encoded\n501\t  surrogates (`ED A0..BF ..`), and values above U+10FFFF are invalid.\n502\t- `\\r` immediately followed by `\\n` -> the `\\r` is dropped (CRLF becomes\n503\t  LF). A lone `\\r` -> `\\x0d`.\n504\t- `\\n` and `\\t` -> kept as is.\n505\t- Other C0 controls (U+0000-U+001F) and DEL (U+007F) -> `\\xNN` (two\n506\t  lowercase hex digits).\n507\t- C1 controls (U+0080-U+009F, valid two-byte UTF-8) -> `\\uNNNN` (four\n508\t  lowercase hex digits, e.g. `\\u009b`).\n509\t- Everything else copied unchanged, including valid U+FFFD and all other\n510\t  non-ASCII text.\n511\t\n512\t**`line(s)`** (single-line): same as `text` except:\n513\t- `\\n` -> the two characters `\\n` (backslash, `n`).\n514\t- `\\t` -> the two characters `\\t`.\n515\t- CRLF is **not** collapsed: `\\r\\n` -> `\\x0d\\n` (escaped CR, then escaped\n516\t  LF as two characters).\n517\t\n518\tProperties: output never contains a C0 control (other than `\\n`/`\\t` in\n519\ttext mode), DEL, a C1 control, or an invalid byte; in line mode it\n520\tcontains no `\\n` or `\\t` at all. Both functions are idempotent (backslash\n521\tis never escaped, and the escapes are printable ASCII).\n522\t\n523\tClean fast path: if the input contains nothing the mode would change,\n524\treturn the input unchanged. Purely an optimization; output is identical.\n525\tIn text mode a CRLF is not clean (the `\\r` must be dropped).\n526\t\n527\tExamples (Go test vectors; left is the raw input, right the output):\n528\t`\"esc\\x1b[2J\"` -> `esc\\x1b[2J`; `\"osc\\x1b]0;title\\x07\"` ->\n529\t`osc\\x1b]0;title\\x07`; `\"nul\\x00 del\\x7f\"` -> `nul\\x00 del\\x7f`;\n530\t`\"lone\\rcarriage return\"` -> `lone\\x0dcarriage return`;\n531\t`\"crlf\\r\\nline\"` -> `\"crlf\\nline\"` (real LF); `\"c1 csi\\u009b2J\"` ->\n532\t`c1 csi\\u009b2J`; raw byte `0x9b` -> `\\x9b`; `\"unicode é ✓ stays\"`\n533\tunchanged. Line mode: `\"desc\\n## X\\r\\n\\tx\\x1b\"` ->\n534\t`desc\\n## X\\x0d\\n\\tx\\x1b` (all escapes literal, one line).\n535\t\n536\t**Call sites** (every one must be preserved):\n537\t\n538\t1. Verifier refuted log line (2.3) -- `line`. The finder severity and\n539\t   truncated description can neither drive the terminal nor add lines.\n540\t2. Markdown single-line fields (2.8): severity, effective severity, drop\n541\t   reason, path, description, alias, CWE, verdict status, verifier name,\n542\t   prior note -- `line`. They cannot start a forged heading or line.\n543\t3. Markdown multi-line fields: reasoning and grounding (via\n544\t   `listItemText`), code quote, fixed code -- `text`. Line structure is\n545\t   kept, controls neutralized.\n546\t4. CLI `logf`, every `roast: <msg>` progress line on stderr -- `text`\n547\t   (not `line`; messages may legitimately span lines). Messages embed\n548\t   repository paths, scope notes, and model names.\n549\t5. CLI human error output (`roast: <error message>`, used when not in\n550\t   JSON error mode) -- `text`. Errors can carry git stderr naming\n551\t   repository paths.\n552\t6. `runs show <id>`: the whole stored `report.md` before it is written to\n553\t   stdout -- `text` over the raw file bytes (`textBytes`). Reports written\n554\t   before rendering escaped text may hold raw control bytes.\n555\t7. `trust` summary: profile selector, profile name, endpoint, protocol,\n556\t   credential, prompt-override name and path -- `line`. Config values are\n557\t   repository-controlled.\n558\t\n559\tJSON output (stdout JSON, `result.json`, JSON error objects) is never\n560\tpassed through `textsafe`.\n561\t\n562\t## 3. TypeScript module design\n563\t\n564\t`src/textsafe/textsafe.ts` (pure, no dependencies):\n565\t\n566\t```ts\n567\texport function text(s:string):string\n568\texport function line(s:string):string\n569\t// Byte-exact Go behavior for raw bytes (runs show, git stderr).\n570\texport function textBytes(b:Uint8Array):string\n571\texport function lineBytes(b:Uint8Array):string\n572\t```\n573\t\n574\t- The string variants iterate code points. A JS string cannot hold invalid\n575\t  UTF-8, but it can hold lone surrogates (for example from `JSON.parse` of\n576\t  `\"\\ud800\"`), which Go never sees (its JSON decoder yields U+FFFD).\n577\t  The llm area turns lone surrogates in model output into U+FFFD when it\n578\t  decodes; `textsafe` escapes any that remain as `\\uNNNN` (lowercase)\n579\t  (spec.md, \"Bytes and text\").\n580\t- The byte variants implement Go's `utf8.DecodeRune` validity rules with a\n581\t  hand-written decoder (do not use `TextDecoder`, which replaces a maximal\n582\t  invalid subpart with one U+FFFD instead of escaping each byte).\n583\t- Fast path: one regex test per mode, for example\n584\t  `/[\\x00-\\x08\\x0b-\\x1f\\x7f-\\x9f\\ud800-\\udfff]/` for text mode (and `\\r`\n585\t  covered by the range), `/[\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f-\\x9f\\ud800-\\udfff]/` for line\n586\t  mode, adjusted so well-formed surrogate pairs stay clean.\n587\t\n588\t`src/gocompat/strings.ts` (shared Go-compatibility helpers; see the\n589\tindex spec, \"Go-compatibility helpers\"):\n590\t\n591\t```ts\n592\texport function isGoSpace(cp:number):boolean\n593\texport function goTrimSpace(s:string):string\n594\texport function goExt(path:string):string\n595\texport function truncateUtf8(s:string, maxBytes:number):string\n596\texport function formatFixed2(x:number):string  // Go \"%.2f\"\n597\t```\n598\t\n599\t`src/verify/verify.ts`:\n600\t\n601\t```ts\n602\timport type { Finding, ReviewResult, Verdict } from '../review/types.js'\n603\timport type { LlmClient, Tool } from '../llm/types.js'\n604\timport type { Ledger } from '../llm/ledger.js'\n605\t\n606\texport interface VerifyDeps {\n607\t    systemPrompt:string;\n608\t    userPrompt?:(f:Finding)=>string;\n609\t    tools:Tool[];\n610\t    maxTurns:number;\n611\t    concurrency?:number;   // default 4\n612\t    log?:(line:string)=>void;\n613\t    maxVerified:number;    // 0 = no cap\n614\t    ledger?:Ledger|null;\n615\t}\n616\t\n617\texport const SUBMIT_VERDICT_TOOL_NAME = 'submit_verdict'\n618\texport const VERDICT_SCHEMA:Record<string, unknown>  // section 2.4\n619\t\n620\texport function verify(\n621\t    signal:AbortSignal,\n622\t    verifier:LlmClient,\n623\t    result:ReviewResult,\n624\t    deps:VerifyDeps\n625\t):Promise<ReviewResult>\n626\t```\n627\t\n628\t- The pool is the shared small promise pool (architecture decision):\n629\t  `limit` workers each `await` the next index from a shared counter and\n630\t  write into a preallocated array, so output order equals input order.\n631\t  Never `Promise.all` all findings at once.\n632\t- `verifyOne` is module-private. It calls the agent loop's `converse` with\n633\t  `finalTool: 'submit_verdict'` and receives the validated final-call\n634\t  arguments as an object. Wrap the entire call in `try/catch`; any thrown\n635\t  error becomes the undecided verdict.\n636\t- The wire verdict is a zod object derived from the same definition as\n637\t  `VERDICT_SCHEMA` if the llm area validates final calls with zod; the\n638\t  transmitted schema must still be exactly the JSON in 2.4 (alphabetical\n639\t  property keys). A test pins it.\n640\t- Depends on: review area types (`Finding`, `Verdict`, `ReviewResult`,\n641\t  `gates`, drop-reason and assessment constants), llm area (`LlmClient`,\n642\t  `Tool`, `converse`, `Ledger.exhausted()`), `textsafe`, `gocompat`.\n643\t\n644\t`src/render/render.ts`:\n645\t\n646\t```ts\n647\texport interface SizeEntry { path:string; bytes:number }\n648\t\n649\texport interface Report {\n650\t    result:ReviewResult;\n651\t    mode:string;\n652\t    filesReviewed:string[]|null;\n653\t    task:string;\n654\t    runId:string;\n655\t    budgets:Record<string, unknown>|null;\n656\t    quick:boolean;\n657\t    verified:boolean;\n658\t    diffTruncated:boolean;\n659\t    originalDiffBytes:number;\n660\t    sizeBreakdown:SizeEntry[];\n661\t    usage:Record<string, Usage>|null;\n662\t    prior:Map<string, string>|null;\n663\t    promptPacks:string[]|null;\n664\t    reviewKind:''|'survey_triage';\n665\t    completion:string;\n666\t    manifestFileCount:number;\n667\t    stopReason:string;\n668\t}\n669\t\n670\texport function toJSON(report:Report):string\n671\texport function toMarkdown(report:Report, showDropped:boolean):string\n672\texport function writeReport(\n673\t    io:{ stdout:Writable; stderr:Writable },\n674\t    format:'json'|'markdown'|'both',\n675\t    showDropped:boolean,\n676\t    report:Report\n677\t):void\n678\t```\n679\t\n680\t- `toJSON` builds plain objects with keys inserted in the documented order\n681\t  (top level alphabetical; finding, verdict, and usage objects in field\n682\t  order; optional keys omitted, never `undefined`) and calls\n683\t  `JSON.stringify` once. Budgets: sort keys recursively before\n684\t  stringifying.\n685\t- `nil` vs empty must be preserved: `files_reviewed`, `notes`,\n686\t  `prompt_packs`, `usage`, and a finding's `lines` serialize `null` when\n687\t  the source was absent and `[]`/`{}` when present but empty;\n688\t  `findings`/`dropped_findings` are always arrays.\n689\t- Depends on: review area (`fingerprint`, `effectiveSeverity`, types), llm\n690\t  area (`Usage`), `textsafe`, `gocompat`.\n691\t\n692\t## 4. Deliberate changes\n693\t\n694\tNone of the listed deliberate changes apply to this area. Debug tracing\n695\t(`roast:verify`, `roast:render`) may be added under decision 5, but must\n696\tnever include finding text, prompts, or verdict bodies.\n697\t\n698\t## 5. Test plan\n699\t\n700\tSeams: `textsafe` and the `gocompat` helpers are tested as units (the\n701\tdecisions allow text sanitization at a low seam). `verify` ordering,\n702\tconcurrency, and ledger behavior are tested with an in-process fake\n703\t`LlmClient` (like Go's stub), because ordering under staggered completion\n704\tis impractical through the CLI. Everything else is tested at the CLI seam\n705\tagainst the `node:http` fake inference server returning `submit_verdict`\n706\ttool calls, asserting on exit codes, stdout JSON, and run-record files.\n707\tMarkdown is pure; test it as a unit on structural properties only (no\n708\texact human text).\n709\t\n710\ttextsafe (unit):\n711\t- Escapes C0, DEL, C1, invalid bytes; keeps `\\n`, `\\t`, valid non-ASCII;\n712\t  CRLF collapses, lone CR escapes (TestTextEscapesControls).\n713\t- Line mode escapes `\\n`, `\\t`, and does not collapse CRLF\n714\t  (TestLineEscapesNewlines).\n715\t- Over every code point U+0000-U+00FF plus bytes `ff fe c2`, outputs of\n716\t  both modes contain no control, no U+FFFD, and line output no `\\n`/`\\t`;\n717\t  both are idempotent (TestOutputHasNoControls). Add a property-based\n718\t  variant over random byte arrays for `textBytes`/`lineBytes`.\n719\t- Lone surrogate handling (new, TS-only; pins the `\\uNNNN` escape).\n720\t\n721\tgocompat (unit): `formatFixed2` on 0.125/0.375/0.625/0.875 matches Go;\n722\t`goTrimSpace` trims U+0085 and not U+FEFF; `truncateUtf8` never splits a\n723\tcode point and measures bytes.\n724\t\n725\tverify (fake client):\n726\t- Confirmed verdict keeps the finding with verdict attached and\n727\t  `verifier` = client name (TestVerify_Confirmed_Kept).\n728\t- Grounded recalibration flows through to the verdict and lowers\n729\t  effective severity (TestVerify_Confirmed_RecalibratedSeverityFlowsThrough).\n730\t- Ungrounded recalibration is cleared\n731\t  (TestVerify_Confirmed_UngroundedRecalibration_Cleared).\n732\t- Grounded refutation moves the finding to dropped with\n733\t  `refuted_by_verifier`, assessment becomes `NO_FINDINGS`\n734\t  (TestVerify_Refuted_Dropped).\n735\t- Loop error -> kept, `undecided`, `insufficient_context`\n736\t  (TestVerify_Error_FailOpen).\n737\t- Output order equals input order when completions arrive in reverse\n738\t  (TestVerify_DeterministicOrder).\n739\t- Existing dropped findings are kept, before new refutations\n740\t  (TestVerify_PreservesExistingDropped).\n741\t- Assessment unchanged when findings remain\n742\t  (TestVerify_AssessmentKeptWhenFindingsRemain).\n743\t- Refutation with whitespace-only grounding fails open\n744\t  (TestVerify_UngroundedRefutation_FailOpen).\n745\t- Refuted log line contains no control characters and keeps escapes\n746\t  visible (TestVerify_RefutedLogEscapesFinderText).\n747\t- New (no Go test): findings at index `>= maxVerified` get the cap\n748\t  verdict without a client call; ledger exhausted before launch yields\n749\t  the budget verdict; never more than `concurrency` calls in flight;\n750\t  `VERDICT_SCHEMA` deep-equals the JSON in 2.4.\n751\t\n752\trender (unit, structural):\n753\t- Survey fields present in JSON only for survey reports; banner present\n754\t  only then (TestSurveyCoverageFields).\n755\t- JSON round-trips, carries a non-empty fingerprint (TestToJSON_RoundTrip).\n756\t- Truncated diff adds `diff_truncated`, `original_diff_bytes`,\n757\t  `size_breakdown` (TestToJSON_DiffTruncatedBlock).\n758\t- Hostile finding text: Markdown holds no raw control or C1 character,\n759\t  escapes stay visible, no line of finding text starts a top-level\n760\t  heading, the code fence is longer than any backtick run inside it; JSON\n761\t  still round-trips the raw description\n762\t  (TestToMarkdown_NeutralizesHostileFindingText).\n763\t- Sort: effective severity desc then confidence desc, stable; assert via\n764\t  alias order in `### ` lines (TestToMarkdown_SortOrder).\n765\t- Dropped section appears only with `showDropped`, findings carry the\n766\t  dropped tag (TestToMarkdown_ShowDropped).\n767\t- Recalibrated severity annotated only when effective differs\n768\t  (TestToMarkdown_RecalibratedSeverityShown,\n769\t  TestToMarkdown_UnrecalibratedSeverityNotAnnotated).\n770\t- Go tests that pin exact headline text (TestToMarkdown_NoFindings,\n771\t  TestToMarkdown_NoDiffSaysNoReviewRan, TestToMarkdown_IncompleteNoSubmission,\n772\t  TestToMarkdown_FindingsHeader, TestToMarkdown_FileAndLines,\n773\t  TestToMarkdown_VerifierGrounding, TestToMarkdown_PriorSighting,\n774\t  TestToMarkdown_PlainFindingUnchanged) are ported as structural checks\n775\t  only (which case is chosen, presence of a verifier/grounding item, the\n776\t  file code span); exact wording is covered by the temporary Go-vs-TS\n777\t  differential harness on `report.md` if the maintainers opt in.\n778\t\n779\tCLI seam:\n780\t- Finder plus verifier against the fake server: `--format json\n781\t  --max-severity HIGH` exits 1, stdout JSON carries `\"status\":\"confirmed\"`,\n782\t  the run record holds finder and verifier responses, `verifier_cap` 0 is\n783\t  recorded (TestFinderVerifierPipelineWithMockEndpoint,\n784\t  TestNativeAnthropicFinderWithChatVerifier).\n785\t- `runs show` escapes control bytes from a stored report\n786\t  (TestRunsShowEscapesStoredReports).\n787\t- Human error output escapes controls (TestWriteErrorEscapesControls).\n788\t- Trust summary escapes controls (TestTrustSummaryEscapesControlCharacters).\n789\t- New: `--quick` and `--no-verify` make no verifier request and report\n790\t  `verified: false`; an undecided verdict without a gate trip exits 4;\n791\t  `--format markdown` writes nothing to stdout; invalid `--format` and\n792\t  `--max-severity` exit 2.\n793\t\n794\t## 6. Go baseline references\n795\t\n796\tAt commit `cd08f10`:\n797\t\n798\t- `internal/verify/verify.go`, `internal/verify/verify_test.go`\n799\t- `internal/render/render.go`, `internal/render/render_test.go`\n800\t- `internal/textsafe/textsafe.go`, `internal/textsafe/textsafe_test.go`\n801\t- `internal/review/types.go` (Severity, Finding, Verdict, `Gates`,\n802\t  `EffectiveSeverity`, drop reasons, assessments, `MaxSeverity`)\n803\t- `internal/llm/llm.go` (`Usage`), `internal/llm/ledger.go`\n804\t  (`Exhausted`, nil-safe), `internal/llm/provider.go` (`Name` = model)\n805\t- `internal/cli/cli.go`: flags (`--format`, `--max-severity`, `--quick`,\n806\t  `--no-verify`, `--max-verified`, `--show-dropped`), `doVerify`, the\n807\t  verify call, report assembly, `writeReport`, `finalizeRunArtifacts`,\n808\t  `reviewExitError`, `logf`, `WriteError`\n809\t- `internal/cli/runs.go` (`runs show`), `internal/cli/trust.go` (summary)\n810\t- Tests: `internal/cli/cli_test.go`\n811\t  (TestFinderVerifierPipelineWithMockEndpoint,\n812\t  TestNativeAnthropicFinderWithChatVerifier),\n813\t  `internal/cli/hardening_test.go` (TestRunsShowEscapesStoredReports,\n814\t  TestWriteErrorEscapesControls), `internal/cli/trust_test.go`\n815\t  (TestTrustSummaryEscapesControlCharacters)\n816\t\n817\t## 7. Resolved\n818\t\n819\tResolved:\n820\t\n821\t1. `\"notes\": null` after verification with no notes: Go parity, kept\n822\t   (spec.md, \"Deliberate changes\").\n823\t2. JSON output is not HTML-escaped; the differential harness compares\n824\t   parsed JSON (spec.md, \"JSON encoding\").\n825\t3. Lone surrogates become U+FFFD when the llm area decodes model output;\n826\t   textsafe escapes any remaining as `\\uNNNN` (spec.md, \"Bytes and text\").\n827\t4. `verified: true` with no findings: Go parity, kept.\n828\t5. Verifier error text in a verdict's reasoning may differ in wording\n829\t   from Go: accepted.\n830\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecb2be46-319d-4607-acba-e6c06893d41b","uuid":"b1ccaa64-d11a-4304-aff5-931aebd2296f","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:50:46.204Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/.claude/projects/-Users-nick-code-roast-ts-rewrite-21-verifier-stage-in-review/ecb2be46-319d-4607-acba-e6c06893d41b/tool-results/buzm1w0v5.txt","content":"# 09 -- Verifier stage, report rendering, text sanitization\n\n## 1. Purpose\n\nThis area covers the three steps between the finder and the run record:\n\n1. The **verifier** stage. Every finding the finder kept is adjudicated by\n   the verifier role's model, which sees the claim and the code only, never\n   the finder's reasoning (anti-anchoring). A refutation counts only when it\n   is grounded in specific code, guards, or language semantics. Anything the\n   verifier cannot decide fails open: the finding keeps gating, with the\n   reason on its verdict.\n2. **Report rendering.** A completed review becomes a JSON payload (stdout,\n   and `result.json` in the run record) and a Markdown summary (stderr, and\n   `report.md` in the run record).\n3. **Text sanitization** (`textsafe`). Finding text comes from a model that\n   read an untrusted repository, so a JSON string such as `\"\\u001b]52;c;...\"`\n   decodes to a real ESC. Every place Roast prints model- or\n   repository-derived text to a terminal or into a human-readable report\n   escapes control characters first. JSON output does not go through it.\n\nOut of scope here (owned by other areas): the finder, prompt texts and the\nverifier user-prompt renderer, exploration tools, the agent loop\n(`Converse`), the token ledger internals, finding fingerprints, prior\nsightings lookup, run-record file writing, and CLI flag parsing in general.\n\nNotation: in quoted output strings below, `{EM}` stands for one literal\nU+2014 EM DASH character, which the Go output contains and the TypeScript\noutput must contain too. `·` is U+00B7 MIDDLE DOT, also literal.\n\n## 2. Behavior contract\n\n### 2.1 Data model used by this area\n\nOwned by the review area; restated here because rendering and verification\ndepend on every field.\n\nSeverity: one of `INFO`, `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `CRITICAL`. `rank`:\nINFO=0, LOW=1, MEDIUM=2, HIGH=3, CRITICAL=4; any other string (including\n`\"\"`) ranks 0. `parseSeverity(s)` upper-cases and trims (Go\n`strings.TrimSpace`), accepts only the five names, rejects `\"\"`.\n\nFinding (JSON field order is significant for output parity):\n\n| key | type | notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reasoning` | string | |\n| `severity` | string | |\n| `confidence` | number | |\n| `cwe` | string | |\n| `description` | string | |\n| `file` | string | |\n| `lines` | int[] or null | `null` when absent |\n| `code_quote` | string | |\n| `fixed_code` | string | |\n| `frontend_category` | string | |\n| `verdict` | Verdict | omitted when absent |\n| `_drop_reason` | string | omitted when `\"\"` |\n| `id` | string | omitted when `\"\"` |\n| `alias` | string | omitted when `\"\"`, e.g. `R-8d8d19` |\n\nVerdict (field order significant):\n\n| key | type | notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `reasoning` | string | always present |\n| `status` | string | `confirmed`, `refuted`, `insufficient_context` |\n| `confidence` | number | always present |\n| `grounding` | string | always present |\n| `recalibrated_severity` | string | omitted when `\"\"` |\n| `verifier` | string | omitted when `\"\"`; set by Roast (model id) |\n| `undecided` | boolean | omitted when false; set by Roast |\n\n`verdict.gates()`: true when the verdict is absent or its status is not\n`refuted`.\n\n`finding.effectiveSeverity()`: the finder's `severity`, unless the verdict\nexists, its status is `confirmed`, `parseSeverity(recalibrated_severity)`\nsucceeds, and that parsed severity's rank is strictly lower than the\nfinder's severity rank; then the parsed (canonical) severity. Severity can\nonly move down, and only on a confirmed verdict.\n\nResult: `findings` (Finding[]), `dropped` (Finding[]), `assessment`\n(string), `notes` (string[] or null), `incomplete` (boolean),\n`stopReason` (string: `\"\"`, `deadline`, `token_budget`,\n`budget_exhausted`).\n\n`result.maxSeverity()`: the highest `effectiveSeverity().rank` among\n`findings` (live findings only), or -1 when there are none.\n\nDrop reasons: `invalid_severity`, `missing_code_quote`,\n`missing_fixed_code`, `ungrounded_code_quote`, `below_confidence_floor`\n(finder side) and `refuted_by_verifier` (this area).\n\nAssessments: `FINDINGS_PRESENT`, `NO_FINDINGS`, `NO_DIFF`,\n`INCOMPLETE_NO_SUBMISSION`, `NO_FINDINGS_IN_SAMPLED_AREAS`.\n\n### 2.2 When verification runs\n\n- `doVerify = !quick && !noVerify` (`--quick`, `--no-verify`, both boolean,\n  default false). When `doVerify` is true the verifier role is validated\n  before anything else runs (config area; failure is a usage error, exit 2).\n  With `--quick` or `--no-verify` the verifier role is never validated or\n  contacted.\n- The verifier client is constructed, and `verify` is called, only when\n  `doVerify` is true **and** the finder returned at least one finding. With\n  zero findings no verifier request is made, but the report still says\n  `\"verified\": true` and `usage` has only a `finder` entry.\n- Before calling `verify`, the CLI logs through its `logf` helper (one\n  `roast: ...` line on stderr, sanitized with `textsafe.text`):\n  `verifying <n> finding(s) with <model> (profile=<p> protocol=<proto>)`.\n- The CLI calls `verify` with: system prompt = the rendered verifier system\n  prompt; user prompt = the verifier user-prompt renderer for the finding\n  (prompts area; it includes the cited file snippet, never the finder's\n  reasoning); tools = the exploration tools over the reviewed tree (context\n  area); `maxTurns = 8`; `maxVerified` = resolved cap; the run's shared\n  token ledger; `log` writes the message plus `\\n` to stderr. Concurrency is\n  not set by the CLI, so the default 4 applies.\n- `maxVerified` resolution: `--max-verified` flag if given on the command\n  line, else `limits.max_verified` from `.roast.json`, else 25. A negative\n  flag value is a usage error `max-verified cannot be negative` (exit 2).\n  `0` means no cap. The resolved value is recorded in budgets as\n  `verifier_cap`.\n- After `verify` returns, `usage.verifier` is the verifier client's usage.\n  The run is **partial** if the finder result was `incomplete` or any\n  surviving finding's verdict has `undecided: true`.\n\n### 2.3 `verify(signal, verifier, result, deps)` algorithm\n\nInputs: `deps.concurrency` (default 4 when `<= 0`), `deps.log` (default\nno-op), `deps.userPrompt` (default returns `\"\"`), `deps.maxVerified`\n(0 = no cap), `deps.ledger` (may be absent; absent is never exhausted).\n\n1. `n = result.findings.length`; allocate `verdicts[n]`.\n2. Run a promise pool of `concurrency` workers over indices `0..n-1`,\n   handed out in ascending index order. For the job at index `i`, at the\n   moment a worker picks it up:\n   1. If `maxVerified > 0 && i >= maxVerified`: verdict =\n      `unverified(\"unverified: over the per-run verifier cap (<maxVerified>)\")`.\n      The cap is by input position, so it is deterministic.\n   2. Else if the ledger is exhausted: verdict =\n      `unverified(\"unverified: run token budget exhausted before this\n      finding's verification\")` (one line in the real string; the\n      apostrophe is U+0027). The check is made at launch only;\n      verifications already in flight finish normally.\n   3. Else: verdict = `verifyOne(finding)`.\n   4. Set `verdict.verifier = verifier.name()` (the verifier role's model\n      id) on every verdict, including unverified and error verdicts.\n   5. Store at `verdicts[i]`.\n   `unverified(reason)` is `{status: \"insufficient_context\", undecided:\n   true, reasoning: reason, confidence: 0, grounding: \"\"}`.\n3. Wait for all workers. Then assemble a **new** result (the input is not\n   mutated):\n   - `dropped` = copy of input `dropped` (existing drops first).\n   - `notes` = copy of input `notes`. Go quirk to preserve: an empty input\n     notes list becomes `null` (Go `append(nil, empty...)` is nil), so a\n     verified run with no notes serializes `\"notes\": null` (kept for\n     Go parity; spec.md).\n   - `assessment`, `incomplete`, `stopReason` copied unchanged (cutoff state\n     survives verification).\n   - `findings` = new empty list.\n4. For each input finding in input order, with `v = verdicts[i]`:\n   1. **Refutation without grounding:** if `v.status == \"refuted\"` and\n      `goTrimSpace(v.grounding) == \"\"`, rewrite `v.status =\n      \"insufficient_context\"`, `v.undecided = true`, `v.reasoning =\n      \"verifier returned refuted without grounding {EM} treating as\n      insufficient_context (fail-open)\"`. Confidence and grounding are\n      kept as returned.\n   2. **Ungrounded recalibration:** if `v.status == \"confirmed\"` and\n      `v.recalibrated_severity != \"\"` and `goTrimSpace(v.grounding) == \"\"`,\n      clear `recalibrated_severity` to `\"\"`.\n   3. Attach `v` as the finding's verdict (copy of the finding).\n   4. If `!v.gates()` (status still `refuted`): set `_drop_reason =\n      \"refuted_by_verifier\"`, append to `dropped`, and call `deps.log` with\n      `roast: verifier refuted [<SEV>] <DESC> (conf <C>)` where\n      `<SEV> = textsafe.line(finding.severity)` (the finder's raw severity),\n      `<DESC> = textsafe.line(truncateUtf8(finding.description, 80))`\n      (truncate first, escape second), and `<C>` is `verdict.confidence`\n      formatted as Go `%.2f` (section 2.9). Log lines are emitted in input\n      order after all verifications finish, not as they complete.\n   5. Else append to `findings`.\n5. If `findings` is empty and `assessment == \"FINDINGS_PRESENT\"`, set\n   `assessment = \"NO_FINDINGS\"`. No other assessment is changed (in\n   particular `INCOMPLETE_NO_SUBMISSION` never becomes `NO_FINDINGS`).\n6. Return the new result. Errors never propagate out of `verify`.\n\nRecalibrated severity is never applied to the finding's `severity` field;\nit lives only on the verdict and takes effect through `effectiveSeverity()`\n(rendering, sort order, `--max-severity`). The JSON output therefore keeps\nthe finder's `severity` and shows `verdict.recalibrated_severity`\nalongside.\n\n`truncateUtf8(s, n)`: if the UTF-8 byte length of `s` is `<= n`, return\n`s`; otherwise cut at byte `n`, moving the cut left while the byte at the\ncut is a UTF-8 continuation byte (`0b10xxxxxx`), so a code point is never\nsplit. Measured in UTF-8 bytes, not UTF-16 units.\n\n### 2.4 `verifyOne(finding)`\n\n- Tools sent: `deps.tools` in order, then the final tool appended last:\n  - name `submit_verdict`\n  - description `Submit your verdict on the finding. Call exactly once.`\n  - no runner (it is the final tool; the agent loop ends on it)\n  - schema: exactly the JSON below (Go reflects it and re-serializes through\n    a map, so property keys are alphabetical in the transmitted bytes):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"confidence\": {\"maximum\": 1, \"minimum\": 0, \"type\": \"number\"},\n    \"grounding\": {\n      \"description\": \"<GROUNDING_DESC>\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n    \"recalibrated_severity\": {\n      \"description\": \"<RECAL_DESC>\",\n      \"enum\": [\"\", \"INFO\", \"LOW\", \"MEDIUM\", \"HIGH\", \"CRITICAL\"],\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"status\": {\n      \"enum\": [\"confirmed\", \"refuted\", \"insufficient_context\"],\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"reasoning\", \"status\", \"confidence\", \"grounding\"],\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n```\n\n  The two placeholders are these exact one-line strings (wrapped here\n  only for width; join the pieces with a single space):\n  - `<GROUNDING_DESC>`: `The exact lines / contradicting code /`\n    `language-semantics fact the verdict rests on`\n  - `<RECAL_DESC>`: `If the finding is real but its severity is`\n    `overstated, the corrected LOWER severity, justified in grounding.`\n    `Leave empty to keep the finder's severity. Never raise severity.`\n    (the apostrophe is U+0027)\n- The model-facing (\"wire\") verdict has only `reasoning`, `status`,\n  `confidence`, `grounding`, `recalibrated_severity`. `verifier` and\n  `undecided` are deliberately absent so the model cannot fabricate them.\n- Call the agent loop: `converse(signal, systemPrompt, userPrompt(finding),\n  {tools, finalTool: \"submit_verdict\", maxTurns: deps.maxTurns})`. A\n  `maxTurns` of 0 means the agent loop's default; the CLI passes 8.\n- On **any** error from the loop (no final call, schema violation of the\n  final call, transport failure after retries, abort):\n  return `{status: \"insufficient_context\", confidence: 0, reasoning:\n  \"verifier did not reach a verdict: \" + err.message, grounding: \"\",\n  undecided: true}`. The finding keeps gating.\n- On success: copy the five wire fields into a verdict\n  (`undecided` false, `verifier` set later by the pool).\n\n### 2.5 Output formats and destinations\n\n`--format` takes `json`, `markdown`, or `both` (default `both`). Any other\nvalue is a usage error `invalid --format \"<value>\"` (Go `%q` quoting),\nexit 2.\n\n`writeReport`:\n- `json` or `both`: `toJSON(report)` plus `\\n` to **stdout**.\n- `markdown` or `both`: `toMarkdown(report, showDropped)` plus `\\n` to\n  **stderr**.\n- JSON is written before Markdown.\n\nRun record (records area writes the files; this area provides content):\n- `result.json` = `toJSON(report)`.\n- `report.md` = `toMarkdown(report, true)` -- dropped findings always\n  included, independent of `--show-dropped`.\n- `writeReport` runs before the run-record files are finalized.\n- After finalization succeeds the CLI logs `run <id> · report <path>`.\n\n`--show-dropped` (boolean, default false) only affects the stderr Markdown.\n\nThere is no color, no ANSI styling, and no TTY detection in rendering;\noutput is identical whether or not stdout/stderr are terminals.\n\nEmpty-scope path (`NO_DIFF`): when scope is empty, no model is called and\nthe CLI writes a report with `result = {assessment: \"NO_DIFF\", findings:\n[], dropped: [], notes: []}`, `mode: \"code\"`, `files_reviewed: []`, all\nother report fields at zero values (no run id, `quick: false`,\n`verified: false` even under `--quick`, `usage` and `prompt_packs` null),\nthrough the same `writeReport`, and exits 0 regardless of\n`--max-severity`. No run record is written.\n\n### 2.6 `--max-severity` and exit codes\n\n- `--max-severity` (string, default `\"\"`). Non-empty values go through\n  `parseSeverity(value.toUpperCase())`; failure is a usage error\n  `invalid --max-severity \"<value>\"` (exit 2). `gateRank` is the parsed\n  rank, or -1 when the flag is empty.\n- Exit decision after the report is written and the run record finalized,\n  in priority order:\n  1. Run-record finalization failed: that error (exit per the CLI error\n     classification area).\n  2. `gateRank >= 0 && result.maxSeverity() >= gateRank`: exit 1\n     (`ExitFindings`). Uses effective (possibly recalibrated) severity of\n     live findings only; dropped and refuted findings never trip it.\n  3. Partial run (section 2.2): exit 4 (`ExitPartial`). Note that findings\n     past the verifier cap or past ledger exhaustion are `undecided`, so\n     they make the run partial.\n  4. Otherwise exit 0.\n\n### 2.7 JSON report (`toJSON`)\n\n`Report` inputs: `result`, `mode`, `filesReviewed`, `task` (not rendered),\n`runId`, `budgets` (object or absent), `quick`, `verified`,\n`diffTruncated`, `originalDiffBytes`, `sizeBreakdown` (`{path, bytes}[]`),\n`usage` (role name -> Usage, or absent), `prior` (fingerprint -> note, or\nabsent), `promptPacks` (string[] or absent), and the survey fields\n`reviewKind` (`\"survey_triage\"` or `\"\"`), `completion` (`partial` |\n`complete`), `manifestFileCount`, `stopReason` (`converged` |\n`budget_exhausted` | `incomplete_no_submission` | `deadline` |\n`token_budget`).\n\nOutput is one compact JSON object (no whitespace, no trailing newline in the\nstring itself). Go emits the top-level keys in **alphabetical order**\n(it marshals a map); the TS version should build the object in the same\nsorted order. Keys:\n\n| key | when present | value |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `assessment` | always | `result.assessment` |\n| `budgets` | `budgets` set | the budgets object, nested keys sorted |\n| `completion` | `reviewKind != \"\"` | `completion` |\n| `diff_truncated` | `diffTruncated` | `true` |\n| `dropped_findings` | always | `result.dropped` as finding-outs, or `[]` |\n| `files_reviewed` | always | `filesReviewed` (`null` if absent) |\n| `findings` | always | finding-out list of `result.findings`, `[]` when empty |\n| `incomplete` | `result.incomplete` | `true` |\n| `manifest_file_count` | `reviewKind != \"\"` | integer |\n| `mode` | always | `mode` (`\"code\"` today) |\n| `notes` | always | `result.notes` (`null` if absent, see 2.3) |\n| `original_diff_bytes` | `diffTruncated` | integer |\n| `prompt_packs` | always | `promptPacks` (`null` if absent) |\n| `quick` | always | boolean |\n| `review_kind` | `reviewKind != \"\"` | `\"survey_triage\"` |\n| `run_id` | `runId != \"\"` | run id |\n| `size_breakdown` | `diffTruncated` | `[{\"path\":..., \"bytes\":...}]` |\n| `stop_reason` | see below | string |\n| `usage` | always | object keyed by role (`finder`, `verifier`), or `null` |\n| `verified` | always | boolean |\n\n`stop_reason`: when `reviewKind != \"\"` it is the report's `stopReason`\n(survey block owns the key, possibly `\"\"`); otherwise it is\n`result.stopReason`, present only when non-empty. A non-survey cut-off run\nwith retained findings thus carries both `incomplete: true` (when the loop\nended without submission) and `stop_reason`.\n\nEach `usage` value: `{\"uncached_input_tokens\":int,\n\"cached_input_tokens\":int, \"cache_write_tokens\":int, \"output_tokens\":int,\n\"calls\":int}` in that order. Role keys sorted.\n\nFinding-out object: the Finding fields in the table order of section 2.1,\nthen:\n- `fingerprint`: the finding's fingerprint (review area), omitted only if\n  empty;\n- `prior_sighting`: `prior[fingerprint]` when `prior` has that key and the\n  note is non-empty (omitted when empty).\n\n`budgets` content is built by the CLI area (`deadline_duration`,\n`request_timeout` as Go duration strings, `max_total_tokens`,\n`verifier_cap`, `max_turns`, `max_attempts`, `max_prompt_bytes`, and\n`ledger_committed_tokens` when the ledger has a limit). The CLI adds\n`ledger_committed_tokens` and sets `prior` after building the report but\nbefore rendering, so both appear in output.\n\nJSON strings are never passed through `textsafe`: the JSON encoder escapes\nC0 controls, so raw finding text round-trips exactly through\n`JSON.parse`. Go's encoder additionally escapes `<`, `>`, `&` as\n`\\u003c`/`\\u003e`/`\\u0026` and U+2028/U+2029; TS does not, and the differential\nharness compares parsed JSON (spec.md, \"JSON encoding\").\nNumbers: Go and JS agree on shortest round-trip float formatting\n(exponent form below 1e-6 and from 1e21, `1e-7` style), so\n`JSON.stringify` numbers match.\n\n### 2.8 Markdown report (`toMarkdown(report, showDropped)`)\n\nLines are collected into a list and joined with `\\n` (no trailing newline\nadded beyond what an empty last line produces). Structure, in order:\n\n1. **Survey banner** (only when `reviewKind != \"\"`):\n   `> Survey triage {EM} manifest contains <manifestFileCount> files,\n   completion=<completion>, stop=<report.stopReason>` (one line), then `\"\"`.\n2. Count `nRefuted` = dropped findings with `_drop_reason ==\n   \"refuted_by_verifier\"`; `nMalformed = dropped.length - nRefuted`.\n3. **Headline.** If `findings` is empty, the first matching case:\n   1. `assessment == \"NO_DIFF\"`: `## Nothing to review in this scope {EM}\n      no review ran`, `\"\"`, then one line (shown wrapped here; the three\n      flag mentions are Markdown code spans with single backticks):\n\n      ```text\n      No model was called, so this is NOT a clean review. Already\n      committed? Try `--base <ref>`; use `--staged` before committing or\n      `--scope repo` for a repository survey.\n      ```\n   2. `result.stopReason` is `deadline` or `token_budget`: `## Roast cut\n      off early (<stopReason>) {EM} no findings before the cutoff`, `\"\"`,\n      `The review was cut short by a run ceiling; this is NOT a clean\n      review.`\n   3. `assessment == \"INCOMPLETE_NO_SUBMISSION\"`: `## Roast incomplete\n      {EM} no findings were submitted`, `\"\"`, `The interactive review\n      exhausted its budget before submitting; this is NOT a clean review.`\n   4. Otherwise: `## Roast complete {EM} no findings`, `\"\"`, then\n      `The adversary found nothing to complain about.`, with\n      ` (<nRefuted> candidate finding(s) were refuted by the cross-model\n      verifier.)` appended on the same line when `nRefuted > 0`.\n\n   If `findings` is non-empty: when `result.stopReason != \"\"`, first\n   `## Roast cut off early (<stopReason>) {EM} partial findings follow`\n   and `\"\"`; then `## Roast: <n> finding(s)` with ` (cross-model\n   verified)` appended when `report.verified`.\n4. If `nMalformed > 0`: `\"\"`, then `*(<nMalformed> candidate(s) dropped by\n   schema gates; --show-dropped to see them.)*`.\n5. `\"\"`.\n6. **Findings**, sorted with a stable sort: effective severity rank\n   descending, then `confidence` descending; ties keep input order. Each\n   rendered with ordinal `i+1` (1-based position after sorting) and\n   `dropped = false`.\n7. **Dropped section**, only when `showDropped` and `dropped` is non-empty:\n   `## Dropped findings (--show-dropped)`, `\"\"`, then each dropped finding\n   in stored order (finder drops first, then verifier refutations), ordinal\n   `i+1`, `dropped = true`.\n\nThe `{EM}` dash in headings and `·` are literal; headline strings are\notherwise plain ASCII. Nothing in the headline is model-derived except\n`stopReason`, which is a fixed internal value.\n\n**Finding block** (`renderFinding(ordinal, finding, dropped, prior)`):\n\n- `sev = line(severity)`; if that is `\"\"`, `sev = \"INFO\"`. If\n  `effectiveSeverity() != severity` (raw string comparison), `sev =\n  \"<line(effective)> (finder claimed <sev> {EM} verifier recalibrated)\"`.\n- `confStr = \" · conf <%.2f confidence>\"`.\n- `tag = \"\"`, or when `dropped`: `\"[DROPPED:<line(reason)>] \"` where\n  reason is `_drop_reason`, or `?` when empty.\n- `path = file`, or `?` when empty (checked before escaping).\n- `ln`: `?` for no lines; `<l0>` for one; `<first>-<last>` for more (first\n  and last elements as given, not min/max).\n- `desc = line(goTrimSpace(description))`.\n- `handle = line(alias)`, or `<ordinal>.` when that is empty.\n- Lines emitted:\n  1. `### <handle> <tag>[<sev><confStr>] <desc>`\n  2. `- **File:** ` + `inlineCode(line(path) + \":\" + ln)`\n  3. only if raw `cwe != \"\"`: `- **CWE:** <line(cwe)>`\n  4. `- **Reasoning:** <listItemText(reasoning, \"  \")>`\n  5. if a verdict exists:\n     `- **Verifier (<line(verifier) or ?>):** <line(status)> (conf <%.2f>)`;\n     then, only if raw `grounding != \"\"`:\n     `  - grounding: <listItemText(grounding, \"    \")>`\n  6. For `(\"Current\", code_quote)` then `(\"Proposed fix\", fixed_code)`:\n     `block = text(value)` with all trailing `\\n` removed. If `block` is\n     non-empty: `- **<label>:**`, then `\"  \" + fence`, then each line of\n     `block` (split on `\\n`) prefixed with two spaces, then\n     `\"  \" + fence`, where `fence = codeFence(block)`. If `block` is empty\n     and `dropped`: `- **<label>:** *(not provided)*`. If empty and not\n     dropped: nothing.\n  7. If `prior` has the finding's fingerprint:\n     `- **Seen previously:** <line(note)>` (emitted even for an empty note).\n  8. `\"\"`.\n\nHelpers:\n- `listItemText(s, indent) = text(goTrimSpace(s))` with every `\\n`\n  replaced by `\\n` + indent, so model text cannot leave its list item and\n  pose as a heading.\n- `codeFence(content)`: backticks repeated `max(3, longestBacktickRun +\n  1)` times, so a quoted backtick run cannot close the block.\n- `inlineCode(s)`: delimiter = backticks repeated `longestBacktickRun(s) +\n  1`; if `s` starts or ends with a backtick, `delim + \" \" + s + \" \" +\n  delim`, else `delim + s + delim`.\n- `longestBacktickRun(s)`: longest run of consecutive `` ` `` characters.\n\n### 2.9 Go-compatible formatting helpers\n\n- `goTrimSpace(s)`: trim leading and trailing characters for which Go\n  `unicode.IsSpace` is true: `\\t \\n \\v \\f \\r`, space, U+0085, U+00A0, and\n  the Unicode `Zs`/line/paragraph separators (U+1680, U+2000-U+200A,\n  U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000). It differs from JS\n  `String.prototype.trim`: Go trims U+0085 (JS does not) and does not trim\n  U+FEFF (JS does). Used for the grounding emptiness checks (2.3) and\n  description/reasoning/grounding rendering (2.8), where parity matters.\n- `formatFixed2(x)` (Go `%.2f`): Go rounds the exact binary value half-to-even,\n  JS `toFixed(2)` rounds exact ties up. They differ only on exact ties,\n  which for doubles are values where `x * 8` is an odd integer (0.125,\n  0.375, 0.625, 0.875, ...): Go `0.12 0.38 0.62 0.88`, JS\n  `0.13 0.38 0.63 0.88`. Implementation: if `Number.isInteger(x * 8) &&\n  (x * 8) % 2 !== 0`, take `n = Math.floor(x * 100)` (exact), add 1 if `n`\n  is odd, and format `n / 100` with `toFixed(2)`; otherwise `x.toFixed(2)`.\n  Handle negatives symmetrically. Used in the verifier log line and in\n  Markdown confidences.\n\n### 2.10 Text sanitization (`textsafe`)\n\nTwo modes over a sequence of decoded code points (Go: UTF-8 bytes):\n\n**`text(s)`** (multi-line):\n- Byte that is not part of a valid UTF-8 sequence -> `\\xNN` (two lowercase\n  hex digits of that byte). Each invalid byte is escaped individually (Go\n  `DecodeRune` returns size 1 for any invalid or truncated sequence, so\n  `\"\\xe2\\x82\"` -> `\\xe2\\x82`). Overlong encodings, UTF-8-encoded\n  surrogates (`ED A0..BF ..`), and values above U+10FFFF are invalid.\n- `\\r` immediately followed by `\\n` -> the `\\r` is dropped (CRLF becomes\n  LF). A lone `\\r` -> `\\x0d`.\n- `\\n` and `\\t` -> kept as is.\n- Other C0 controls (U+0000-U+001F) and DEL (U+007F) -> `\\xNN` (two\n  lowercase hex digits).\n- C1 controls (U+0080-U+009F, valid two-byte UTF-8) -> `\\uNNNN` (four\n  lowercase hex digits, e.g. `\\u009b`).\n- Everything else copied unchanged, including valid U+FFFD and all other\n  non-ASCII text.\n\n**`line(s)`** (single-line): same as `text` except:\n- `\\n` -> the two characters `\\n` (backslash, `n`).\n- `\\t` -> the two characters `\\t`.\n- CRLF is **not** collapsed: `\\r\\n` -> `\\x0d\\n` (escaped CR, then escaped\n  LF as two characters).\n\nProperties: output never contains a C0 control (other than `\\n`/`\\t` in\ntext mode), DEL, a C1 control, or an invalid byte; in line mode it\ncontains no `\\n` or `\\t` at all. Both functions are idempotent (backslash\nis never escaped, and the escapes are printable ASCII).\n\nClean fast path: if the input contains nothing the mode would change,\nreturn the input unchanged. Purely an optimization; output is identical.\nIn text mode a CRLF is not clean (the `\\r` must be dropped).\n\nExamples (Go test vectors; left is the raw input, right the output):\n`\"esc\\x1b[2J\"` -> `esc\\x1b[2J`; `\"osc\\x1b]0;title\\x07\"` ->\n`osc\\x1b]0;title\\x07`; `\"nul\\x00 del\\x7f\"` -> `nul\\x00 del\\x7f`;\n`\"lone\\rcarriage return\"` -> `lone\\x0dcarriage return`;\n`\"crlf\\r\\nline\"` -> `\"crlf\\nline\"` (real LF); `\"c1 csi\\u009b2J\"` ->\n`c1 csi\\u009b2J`; raw byte `0x9b` -> `\\x9b`; `\"unicode é ✓ stays\"`\nunchanged. Line mode: `\"desc\\n## X\\r\\n\\tx\\x1b\"` ->\n`desc\\n## X\\x0d\\n\\tx\\x1b` (all escapes literal, one line).\n\n**Call sites** (every one must be preserved):\n\n1. Verifier refuted log line (2.3) -- `line`. The finder severity and\n   truncated description can neither drive the terminal nor add lines.\n2. Markdown single-line fields (2.8): severity, effective severity, drop\n   reason, path, description, alias, CWE, verdict status, verifier name,\n   prior note -- `line`. They cannot start a forged heading or line.\n3. Markdown multi-line fields: reasoning and grounding (via\n   `listItemText`), code quote, fixed code -- `text`. Line structure is\n   kept, controls neutralized.\n4. CLI `logf`, every `roast: <msg>` progress line on stderr -- `text`\n   (not `line`; messages may legitimately span lines). Messages embed\n   repository paths, scope notes, and model names.\n5. CLI human error output (`roast: <error message>`, used when not in\n   JSON error mode) -- `text`. Errors can carry git stderr naming\n   repository paths.\n6. `runs show <id>`: the whole stored `report.md` before it is written to\n   stdout -- `text` over the raw file bytes (`textBytes`). Reports written\n   before rendering escaped text may hold raw control bytes.\n7. `trust` summary: profile selector, profile name, endpoint, protocol,\n   credential, prompt-override name and path -- `line`. Config values are\n   repository-controlled.\n\nJSON output (stdout JSON, `result.json`, JSON error objects) is never\npassed through `textsafe`.\n\n## 3. TypeScript module design\n\n`src/textsafe/textsafe.ts` (pure, no dependencies):\n\n```ts\nexport function text(s:string):string\nexport function line(s:string):string\n// Byte-exact Go behavior for raw bytes (runs show, git stderr).\nexport function textBytes(b:Uint8Array):string\nexport function lineBytes(b:Uint8Array):string\n```\n\n- The string variants iterate code points. A JS string cannot hold invalid\n  UTF-8, but it can hold lone surrogates (for example from `JSON.parse` of\n  `\"\\ud800\"`), which Go never sees (its JSON decoder yields U+FFFD).\n  The llm area turns lone surrogates in model output into U+FFFD when it\n  decodes; `textsafe` escapes any that remain as `\\uNNNN` (lowercase)\n  (spec.md, \"Bytes and text\").\n- The byte variants implement Go's `utf8.DecodeRune` validity rules with a\n  hand-written decoder (do not use `TextDecoder`, which replaces a maximal\n  invalid subpart with one U+FFFD instead of escaping each byte).\n- Fast path: one regex test per mode, for example\n  `/[\\x00-\\x08\\x0b-\\x1f\\x7f-\\x9f\\ud800-\\udfff]/` for text mode (and `\\r`\n  covered by the range), `/[\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f-\\x9f\\ud800-\\udfff]/` for line\n  mode, adjusted so well-formed surrogate pairs stay clean.\n\n`src/gocompat/strings.ts` (shared Go-compatibility helpers; see the\nindex spec, \"Go-compatibility helpers\"):\n\n```ts\nexport function isGoSpace(cp:number):boolean\nexport function goTrimSpace(s:string):string\nexport function goExt(path:string):string\nexport function truncateUtf8(s:string, maxBytes:number):string\nexport function formatFixed2(x:number):string  // Go \"%.2f\"\n```\n\n`src/verify/verify.ts`:\n\n```ts\nimport type { Finding, ReviewResult, Verdict } from '../review/types.js'\nimport type { LlmClient, Tool } from '../llm/types.js'\nimport type { Ledger } from '../llm/ledger.js'\n\nexport interface VerifyDeps {\n    systemPrompt:string;\n    userPrompt?:(f:Finding)=>string;\n    tools:Tool[];\n    maxTurns:number;\n    concurrency?:number;   // default 4\n    log?:(line:string)=>void;\n    maxVerified:number;    // 0 = no cap\n    ledger?:Ledger|null;\n}\n\nexport const SUBMIT_VERDICT_TOOL_NAME = 'submit_verdict'\nexport const VERDICT_SCHEMA:Record<string, unknown>  // section 2.4\n\nexport function verify(\n    signal:AbortSignal,\n    verifier:LlmClient,\n    result:ReviewResult,\n    deps:VerifyDeps\n):Promise<ReviewResult>\n```\n\n- The pool is the shared small promise pool (architecture decision):\n  `limit` workers each `await` the next index from a shared counter and\n  write into a preallocated array, so output order equals input order.\n  Never `Promise.all` all findings at once.\n- `verifyOne` is module-private. It calls the agent loop's `converse` with\n  `finalTool: 'submit_verdict'` and receives the validated final-call\n  arguments as an object. Wrap the entire call in `try/catch`; any thrown\n  error becomes the undecided verdict.\n- The wire verdict is a zod object derived from the same definition as\n  `VERDICT_SCHEMA` if the llm area validates final calls with zod; the\n  transmitted schema must still be exactly the JSON in 2.4 (alphabetical\n  property keys). A test pins it.\n- Depends on: review area types (`Finding`, `Verdict`, `ReviewResult`,\n  `gates`, drop-reason and assessment constants), llm area (`LlmClient`,\n  `Tool`, `converse`, `Ledger.exhausted()`), `textsafe`, `gocompat`.\n\n`src/render/render.ts`:\n\n```ts\nexport interface SizeEntry { path:string; bytes:number }\n\nexport interface Report {\n    result:ReviewResult;\n    mode:string;\n    filesReviewed:string[]|null;\n    task:string;\n    runId:string;\n    budgets:Record<string, unknown>|null;\n    quick:boolean;\n    verified:boolean;\n    diffTruncated:boolean;\n    originalDiffBytes:number;\n    sizeBreakdown:SizeEntry[];\n    usage:Record<string, Usage>|null;\n    prior:Map<string, string>|null;\n    promptPacks:string[]|null;\n    reviewKind:''|'survey_triage';\n    completion:string;\n    manifestFileCount:number;\n    stopReason:string;\n}\n\nexport function toJSON(report:Report):string\nexport function toMarkdown(report:Report, showDropped:boolean):string\nexport function writeReport(\n    io:{ stdout:Writable; stderr:Writable },\n    format:'json'|'markdown'|'both',\n    showDropped:boolean,\n    report:Report\n):void\n```\n\n- `toJSON` builds plain objects with keys inserted in the documented order\n  (top level alphabetical; finding, verdict, and usage objects in field\n  order; optional keys omitted, never `undefined`) and calls\n  `JSON.stringify` once. Budgets: sort keys recursively before\n  stringifying.\n- `nil` vs empty must be preserved: `files_reviewed`, `notes`,\n  `prompt_packs`, `usage`, and a finding's `lines` serialize `null` when\n  the source was absent and `[]`/`{}` when present but empty;\n  `findings`/`dropped_findings` are always arrays.\n- Depends on: review area (`fingerprint`, `effectiveSeverity`, types), llm\n  area (`Usage`), `textsafe`, `gocompat`.\n\n## 4. Deliberate changes\n\nNone of the listed deliberate changes apply to this area. Debug tracing\n(`roast:verify`, `roast:render`) may be added under decision 5, but must\nnever include finding text, prompts, or verdict bodies.\n\n## 5. Test plan\n\nSeams: `textsafe` and the `gocompat` helpers are tested as units (the\ndecisions allow text sanitization at a low seam). `verify` ordering,\nconcurrency, and ledger behavior are tested with an in-process fake\n`LlmClient` (like Go's stub), because ordering under staggered completion\nis impractical through the CLI. Everything else is tested at the CLI seam\nagainst the `node:http` fake inference server returning `submit_verdict`\ntool calls, asserting on exit codes, stdout JSON, and run-record files.\nMarkdown is pure; test it as a unit on structural properties only (no\nexact human text).\n\ntextsafe (unit):\n- Escapes C0, DEL, C1, invalid bytes; keeps `\\n`, `\\t`, valid non-ASCII;\n  CRLF collapses, lone CR escapes (TestTextEscapesControls).\n- Line mode escapes `\\n`, `\\t`, and does not collapse CRLF\n  (TestLineEscapesNewlines).\n- Over every code point U+0000-U+00FF plus bytes `ff fe c2`, outputs of\n  both modes contain no control, no U+FFFD, and line output no `\\n`/`\\t`;\n  both are idempotent (TestOutputHasNoControls). Add a property-based\n  variant over random byte arrays for `textBytes`/`lineBytes`.\n- Lone surrogate handling (new, TS-only; pins the `\\uNNNN` escape).\n\ngocompat (unit): `formatFixed2` on 0.125/0.375/0.625/0.875 matches Go;\n`goTrimSpace` trims U+0085 and not U+FEFF; `truncateUtf8` never splits a\ncode point and measures bytes.\n\nverify (fake client):\n- Confirmed verdict keeps the finding with verdict attached and\n  `verifier` = client name (TestVerify_Confirmed_Kept).\n- Grounded recalibration flows through to the verdict and lowers\n  effective severity (TestVerify_Confirmed_RecalibratedSeverityFlowsThrough).\n- Ungrounded recalibration is cleared\n  (TestVerify_Confirmed_UngroundedRecalibration_Cleared).\n- Grounded refutation moves the finding to dropped with\n  `refuted_by_verifier`, assessment becomes `NO_FINDINGS`\n  (TestVerify_Refuted_Dropped).\n- Loop error -> kept, `undecided`, `insufficient_context`\n  (TestVerify_Error_FailOpen).\n- Output order equals input order when completions arrive in reverse\n  (TestVerify_DeterministicOrder).\n- Existing dropped findings are kept, before new refutations\n  (TestVerify_PreservesExistingDropped).\n- Assessment unchanged when findings remain\n  (TestVerify_AssessmentKeptWhenFindingsRemain).\n- Refutation with whitespace-only grounding fails open\n  (TestVerify_UngroundedRefutation_FailOpen).\n- Refuted log line contains no control characters and keeps escapes\n  visible (TestVerify_RefutedLogEscapesFinderText).\n- New (no Go test): findings at index `>= maxVerified` get the cap\n  verdict without a client call; ledger exhausted before launch yields\n  the budget verdict; never more than `concurrency` calls in flight;\n  `VERDICT_SCHEMA` deep-equals the JSON in 2.4.\n\nrender (unit, structural):\n- Survey fields present in JSON only for survey reports; banner present\n  only then (TestSurveyCoverageFields).\n- JSON round-trips, carries a non-empty fingerprint (TestToJSON_RoundTrip).\n- Truncated diff adds `diff_truncated`, `original_diff_bytes`,\n  `size_breakdown` (TestToJSON_DiffTruncatedBlock).\n- Hostile finding text: Markdown holds no raw control or C1 character,\n  escapes stay visible, no line of finding text starts a top-level\n  heading, the code fence is longer than any backtick run inside it; JSON\n  still round-trips the raw description\n  (TestToMarkdown_NeutralizesHostileFindingText).\n- Sort: effective severity desc then confidence desc, stable; assert via\n  alias order in `### ` lines (TestToMarkdown_SortOrder).\n- Dropped section appears only with `showDropped`, findings carry the\n  dropped tag (TestToMarkdown_ShowDropped).\n- Recalibrated severity annotated only when effective differs\n  (TestToMarkdown_RecalibratedSeverityShown,\n  TestToMarkdown_UnrecalibratedSeverityNotAnnotated).\n- Go tests that pin exact headline text (TestToMarkdown_NoFindings,\n  TestToMarkdown_NoDiffSaysNoReviewRan, TestToMarkdown_IncompleteNoSubmission,\n  TestToMarkdown_FindingsHeader, TestToMarkdown_FileAndLines,\n  TestToMarkdown_VerifierGrounding, TestToMarkdown_PriorSighting,\n  TestToMarkdown_PlainFindingUnchanged) are ported as structural checks\n  only (which case is chosen, presence of a verifier/grounding item, the\n  file code span); exact wording is covered by the temporary Go-vs-TS\n  differential harness on `report.md` if the maintainers opt in.\n\nCLI seam:\n- Finder plus verifier against the fake server: `--format json\n  --max-severity HIGH` exits 1, stdout JSON carries `\"status\":\"confirmed\"`,\n  the run record holds finder and verifier responses, `verifier_cap` 0 is\n  recorded (TestFinderVerifierPipelineWithMockEndpoint,\n  TestNativeAnthropicFinderWithChatVerifier).\n- `runs show` escapes control bytes from a stored report\n  (TestRunsShowEscapesStoredReports).\n- Human error output escapes controls (TestWriteErrorEscapesControls).\n- Trust summary escapes controls (TestTrustSummaryEscapesControlCharacters).\n- New: `--quick` and `--no-verify` make no verifier request and report\n  `verified: false`; an undecided verdict without a gate trip exits 4;\n  `--format markdown` writes nothing to stdout; invalid `--format` and\n  `--max-severity` exit 2.\n\n## 6. Go baseline references\n\nAt commit `cd08f10`:\n\n- `internal/verify/verify.go`, `internal/verify/verify_test.go`\n- `internal/render/render.go`, `internal/render/render_test.go`\n- `internal/textsafe/textsafe.go`, `internal/textsafe/textsafe_test.go`\n- `internal/review/types.go` (Severity, Finding, Verdict, `Gates`,\n  `EffectiveSeverity`, drop reasons, assessments, `MaxSeverity`)\n- `internal/llm/llm.go` (`Usage`), `internal/llm/ledger.go`\n  (`Exhausted`, nil-safe), `internal/llm/provider.go` (`Name` = model)\n- `internal/cli/cli.go`: flags (`--format`, `--max-severity`, `--quick`,\n  `--no-verify`, `--max-verified`, `--show-dropped`), `doVerify`, the\n  verify call, report assembly, `writeReport`, `finalizeRunArtifacts`,\n  `reviewExitError`, `logf`, `WriteError`\n- `internal/cli/runs.go` (`runs show`), `internal/cli/trust.go` (summary)\n- Tests: `internal/cli/cli_test.go`\n  (TestFinderVerifierPipelineWithMockEndpoint,\n  TestNativeAnthropicFinderWithChatVerifier),\n  `internal/cli/hardening_test.go` (TestRunsShowEscapesStoredReports,\n  TestWriteErrorEscapesControls), `internal/cli/trust_test.go`\n  (TestTrustSummaryEscapesControlCharacters)\n\n## 7. Resolved\n\nResolved:\n\n1. `\"notes\": null` after verification with no notes: Go parity, kept\n   (spec.md, \"Deliberate changes\").\n2. JSON output is not HTML-escaped; the differential harness compares\n   parsed JSON (spec.md, \"JSON encoding\").\n3. Lone surrogates become U+FFFD when the llm area decodes model output;\n   textsafe escapes any remaining as `\\uNNNN` (spec.md, \"Bytes and text\").\n4. `verified: true` with no findings: Go parity, kept.\n5. Verifier error text in a verdict's reasoning may differ in wording\n   from Go: accepted.\n","numLines":830,"startLine":1,"totalLines":830}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012NE9DQKWmfafMJ3CK19tpg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
