rified: false`; a run with zero findings and verification on makes no verifier request and reports `verified: true` with only a `finder` usage entry.\n[x] Without `--no-verify`, an invalid verifier role exits 2 with zero requests; with `--no-verify` the same config reviews.\n[x] `--max-verified 1` with two findings sends one verifier conversation and the second finding's verdict is undecided (exit 4).\n[x] The verifier request's tool list ends with `submit_verdict` after the exploration tools.\n[x] Aborting `io.signal` during verification still writes `result.json.gz` and `report.md` and exits 4.\n[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n`npx roast review` now runs the verifier stage after the finder. All checklist items pass. `npm test` passes (6797 assertions), lint is clean, `go build` succeeds, and `npm run test:go` passes. On the first Go run, `TestOpenRouterLoginStoresTheMintedKeyForTheProject` failed once with an EOF on the login callback. No Go code changed, and it passed on every rerun, so it looks like an existing flaky test.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **`src/verify/verify.ts`:** checks each finding with the verifier model, up to 4 at a time. Results come back in input order. It never throws: a failed check, a loop error, or a Ctrl-C each leave the finding in the report marked undecided.\n- **`src/cli/review.ts` (step 17):** the verifier client is only created when verification is on and there is at least one finding. The verifier always gets the read/list/grep tools, even when the finder ran without them. Its token usage goes into the report and `meta.json`. Any undecided finding makes the run partial (exit 4).\n\n**Choices worth checking:**\n- **`notes` type:** Go turns an empty notes list into `null` after verification. Making the shared result type allow `null` broke the finder in several places. So `verify` returns its own `VerifiedResult` type instead, and the rest of the review code uses that.\n- **Async user prompt:** the spec gives `userPrompt` as synchronous, but reading the cited file is async. I made it allowed to return a promise. If it fails, that finding gets the undecided result like any other error.\n- **Invalid-key test:** `ROAST_VERIFIER_API_KEY` works as a fallback key for any profile. To make the verifier role invalid, the test also has to delete it from the environment.\n\n**Process note:** for the `verify` module I wrote the tests and the code together. The tests first failed only because the module didn't exist yet, not on behavior. The CLI tests did fail on real behavior before I added step 17.\n\nThere are two commits: `413d219` (the module) and `6c655f1` (CLI step 17 and its tests). I added area notes to `docs/agents/typescript.md`. My working notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1384,"cache_read_input_tokens":151336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1384},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecb2be46-319d-4607-acba-e6c06893d41b","uuid":"641d7d7f-7653-4831-9bfb-248a0e244bf6","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:01:01.290Z","request_id":"req_011ChLvmomNv8G5brFoGAS5Z"}
